{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaRows","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormulaRows","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.dimHLF_column","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.dimHLF_column","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L256-L263","doc":"**`dimHLF` of a single column is `1`.** `n!/n! = 1`: there is exactly one standard\nYoung tableau of shape `[1,1,…,1]`, since the entries must ascend down the column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_column","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_column","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L240-L254","doc":"**The single-column hook product is `n!`.** The column `[1,1,…,1]` has one cell per\nrow, and the hook at row `i` is `(1 - 0) + (n - i) - 1 = n - i`, so the product over\n`i < n` is the descending product `n · (n-1) ⋯ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_column","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_column","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L228-L238","doc":"`colLen` of a single column is `n` at column `0` and `0` beyond: every one of the `n`\nparts exceeds `0`, and none exceeds `0 + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_mul","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L198-L217","doc":"**Two-row hook product, divisor-free closed form (sorry-free).** For `a ≥ b ≥ 1`,\n`prodHooks [a,b] · (a + 1 − b)! = (a+1)! · (a − b)! · b!`.  This is the Frame–Robinson–Thrall\nhook product on a two-row shape, the denominator of the ballot-number dimension\n`dimHLF [a,b] = (a+b)! · (a+1−b)! / ((a+1)! · (a−b)! · b!)` (equivalently the standard\n`(a+b)!·(a−b+1)/((a+1)·a!·b!)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_row0_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_row0_mul","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L157-L196","doc":"Row-0 hook product of `[a,b]` (`a ≥ b`) in divisor-free form:\n`(∏_{j} h(0,j)) · (a + 1 − b)! = (a+1)! · (a − b)!`.  The row-0 hooks split as\n`a + 1 − j` for `j < b` and `a − j` for `b ≤ j < a`; the first block contributes the\ndescending product `(a+1)!/(a+1−b)!`, the second `(a − b)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_row1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_pair_row1","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L143-L155","doc":"Row-1 hook product of `[a,b]` (`a ≥ b`): cell `j < b` of the second row has hook\n`(b − j) + (colLen j − 1) − 1 = b − j` (since `j < b ⟹ colLen = 2`), so the product is `b!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_desc_mul_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_desc_mul_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L123-L139","doc":"Divisor-free ascending product: `(∏_{j < b} (N − j)) · (N − b)! = N!` for `b ≤ N`.\nThe `b` largest descending factors of `N!` times the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range'_descending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range'_descending","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L114-L121","doc":"The descending tail product `∏_{j ∈ [b,a)} (a − j) = (a − b)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range_split","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L101-L112","doc":"Split a `range a` product at `b ≤ a` into the `[0,b)` prefix and the `[b,a)` tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.dimHLF_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.dimHLF_single","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L90-L97","doc":"**One-row dimension (sorry-free).** `dimHLF [a] = 1` for every `a ≥ 1`: there is exactly\none standard Young tableau of a single row.  (`a = 0` gives the empty shape with `dimHLF = 1`\nas well, since `0!/1 = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prodHooks_single","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L74-L88","doc":"**One-row hook product (sorry-free).** `prodHooks [a] = a!`: the hook of cell `j`\n(`j < a`) of a single row is `(a − j) + (colLen j − 0) − 1 = a − j`, and the descending\nproduct is `a!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_pair","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L59-L70","doc":"The column-count of a two-row shape `[a,b]` with `a ≥ b`:\n`colLen [a,b] j = 2` for `j < b`, `1` for `b ≤ j < a`, `0` for `a ≤ j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.colLen_single","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L53-L57","doc":"The column-count of a one-row shape: `colLen [a] j = 1` iff `j < a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range_descending","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookRows.prod_range_descending","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTHookFormulaRows.lean#L39-L49","doc":"`∏_{j < a} (a − j) = a!` — the descending product is the factorial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}